<BR>
<BR>
<BR>
<DIV ALIGN='center'>
<FONT SIZE="+2"><B>Downloading MacTeX 2025</B></FONT>
</DIV>
<BR>

<p> MacTeX-2025 requires macOS 10.14 or higher. These systems are named Mojave, Catalina, Big Sur, Monterey, Ventura, Sonoma, and Sequoia.  It runs natively on both Arm and Intel machines. The same source code is used to compile both types of code, so Apple's Arm and Intel machines are on exactly the same footing. All install packages are  developer-signed and notarized by Apple. 

<p> One  program, asymptote, does not run on Mojave but runs on Catalina and higher. 
This program is a recent addition to TeX Live and was seldom used on Mojave.

<p> Click the link below to download. <!-- Download with Safari <I>strongly recommended</I>. -->
While downloading, please skim the rest of the page.
Users who run into trouble sometimes write us without noticing that the solution is on this very page.  



<p><center>
<a href="https://mirror.ctan.org/systems/mac/mactex/MacTeX.pkg"><b>MacTeX.pkg</b></a>.
</center>
<!--
WARNING: The link below leads to a multiplexer which connects to
various CTAN servers. For the first few days of a release, these servers provide
MacTeX-2021 rather than the new release. Wait a few days 
after 2025/04/03 before downloading.
-->
<p><center>The Size is   
6.4G	- 27 February 2026

</center>
